# Session 3.1 — added to fix a real problem found this session: Kalshi's
# raw market-data snapshot hit ~51 MB at a real run's market count (60,000
# markets), right at GitHub's 50 MB warning line and on track to cross its
# 100 MB hard push limit as this project's caps are raised further. Every
# ingestion run also creates a NEW, separately-named raw file (see
# ingest_kalshi.py / ingest_polymarket.py's save_raw_snapshot functions),
# so committing these forever grows the repo, run after run, even if any
# single file stays under the limit.
#
# DECISION (2026-09-04): raw JSON snapshots for exchange-style venues
# (Kalshi, Polymarket) are still written locally every run — kept for
# debugging a future schema change, the same reason Session 2.2's
# ingest_pickem.py saves raw snapshots for the pick'em platforms — but are
# no longer committed to the repo. The normalized CSV (a small fraction of
# the raw size, since it keeps only the 14 fields this project actually
# uses) remains the real, committed historical record for these venues.
# This is a deliberate, named deviation from Session 2.2's original
# "commit raw + normalized every run" pattern, not a silent one — that
# pattern was built around the pick'em platforms' much smaller real data
# volume and does not scale to an exchange with tens of thousands of
# open markets.
data/exchange/raw/

# Standard Python housekeeping — not yet present in this repo, added
# alongside the entry above since a .gitignore did not exist before this
# session.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
